   "notes": "18 King's Parade (no addr in OSM building; OSM shop node 18 = University of Cambridge Museums Shop). Ornate mock-Tudor timber front: leaded diamond-lattice canted oriels on the 1st and 2nd floors in the northern ~3 m, carved/moulded plaster panels under the oriels, a narrow leaded light beside the 1st-floor oriel, and in the southern part a jettied box with X-braced (St Andrew's cross) timbering and a carved plaster panel at its base rising into an X-braced gable; dormer above. Dark navy shopfront 'MUSEUMS' with University crest. Layout read from oblique views only."
